chnology","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1509-4553","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.26636/jtit.2023.4.1336","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.26636/jtit.2023.4.1336","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.26636/jtit.2023.4.1336","url":"https://doi.org/10.26636/jtit.2023.4.1336","query":"universal fake image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:04:26Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e3720329ce2d6bae","title":"Detect Any Deepfakes: Segment Anything Meets Face Forgery Detection and Localization","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"2023-06-29","abstract":"The rapid advancements in computer vision have stimulated remarkable progress in face forgery techniques, capturing the dedicated attention of researchers committed to detecting forgeries and precisely localizing manipulated areas. Nonetheless, with limited fine-grained pixel-wise supervision labels, deepfake detection models perform unsatisfactorily on precise forgery detection and localization. To address this challenge, we introduce the well-trained vision segmentation foundation model, i.e., Segment Anything Model (SAM) in face forgery detection and localization. Based on SAM, we propose the Detect Any Deepfakes (DADF) framework with the Multiscale Adapter, which can capture short- and long-range forgery contexts for efficient fine-tuning. Moreover, to better identify forged traces and augment the model's sensitivity towards forgery regions, Reconstruction Guided Attention (RGA) module is proposed. The proposed framework seamlessly integrates end-to-end forgery localization and detection optimization. Extensive experiments on three benchmark datasets demonstrate the superiority of our approach for both forgery detection and localization. The codes will be released soon at https://github.com/laiyingxin2/DADF.","authors":[{"id":"a5061194131","name":"Yingxin Lai","orcid":"0000-0003-1369-2205","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5072443458","name":"Zhiming Luo","orcid":"0000-0002-3411-9582","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5062522283","name":"Zitong Yu","orcid":"0000-0001-6505-3304","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-14849488429a12","name":"arXiv (Cornell University)","short_name":"","type":"preprint","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2306.17075","arxiv_id":"2306.17075","openalex_id":"W4382766508","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2306.17075","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4382766508","url":"https://openalex.org/W4382766508","query":"scene text image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-d0ab706a241e68ae","title":"Medical image watermarking: a survey on applications, approach and performance requirement compliance","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"2023-09-12","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5088063830","name":"Shehu Ayuba","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i139322472","i4210152770"]},{"id":"a5045219052","name":"Wan Mohd Nazmee Wan Zainon","orcid":"0000-0003-3810-5919","institution_ids":["i139322472"]}],"institution_ids":["i139322472","i4210152770"],"venue":{"id":"venue-930c422d540cf4","name":"International Journal of Multimedia Information Retrieval","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/s13735-023-00290-9","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4386624975","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13735-023-00290-9","citation_count":14,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4386624975","url":"https://openalex.org/W4386624975","query":"image watermarking survey","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/s13735-023-00290-9","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13735-023-00290-9","query":"image watermarking survey","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:33:43Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e6ca420c442790ae","title":"Rotation Angle Detection Using a Pilot Signal from Rotated Stego-Image","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-febbc622c9a39a","name":"Rinka Kawano","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-05dd3b1bffb852","name":"Masaki Kawamura","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-4991c0e4557b16","name":"2023 Asia Pacific Signal and Information Processing Association Annual Summit and Conference (APSIPA ASC)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/apsipaasc58517.2023.10317506","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/apsipaasc58517.2023.10317506","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/apsipaasc58517.2023.10317506","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/apsipaasc58517.2023.10317506","query":"cover stego image classification","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:33:14Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-62442390365604ae","title":"Countering Spoof: Towards Detecting Deepfake with Multidimensional Biological Signals","title_zh":"","year":2021,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-8a7e35f8e2cfa3","name":"Xinlei Jin","orcid":"0000-0002-3991-1405","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-5c9492534c7e50","name":"Dengpan Ye","orcid":"0000-0003-2510-9523","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-96d15391143157","name":"Chuanxi Chen","orcid":"0000-0002-3863-0417","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-c2cec5c5bca959","name":"Security and Communication Networks","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1939-0122","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1155/2021/6626974","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2021/6626974","citation_count":15,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1155/2021/6626974","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2021/6626974","query":"deepfake image detection @ USENIX Security","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:22Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e1d51cbcd6adc5ae","title":"GAN-based spatial image steganography with cross feedback mechanism","title_zh":"","year":2021,"publication_date":"2021-09-27","abstract":"Abstract Steganography has been widely used to realize covert communication with multimedia content. By simulating the competition between a generator and a discriminator in a generative adversarial network (GAN), good distortion measurement can be automatically learnt to help designing high undetectable steganography. Nevertheless, existing GAN-based steganography always uses linear convolutional neural networks to construct generators, where the modification information of pixel in deep layers cannot be real-time transmitted to the neurons of the shallow layers, resulting in a low undetectable performance due to insufficient network training. To address the problem, we propose a new GAN-based spatial steganographic scheme. Different from existing GAN-based steganography, we build multiple cross feedback channels between the contraction path and the expansion path of the generator, which allows that the down-sampling information is directly sent to the expansion layer through these feedback channels. Since the detailed information from deep layers can be captured effectively by referring to the information from cover image, the generator can finally learn a sophisticated probability map to guide high undetectable steganography. Comprehensive experimental results demonstrate that, with the same steganalyzers, our scheme is superior to existing GAN-based steganographic schemes in terms of anti-steganalysis capability.","authors":[{"id":"a5001193910","name":"Fengyong Li","orcid":"0000-0002-3385-8164","institution_ids":["i23632641"]},{"id":"a5049199665","name":"Zongliang Yu","orcid":"0000-0002-5808-269X","institution_ids":["i23632641"]},{"id":"a5072469414","name":"Chuan Qin","orcid":"0000-0002-0370-4623","institution_ids":["i148128674"]}],"institution_ids":["i148128674","i23632641"],"venue":{"id":"venue-d4a91ed12e0234","name":"Signal Processing","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.sigpro.2021.108341","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3202332855","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sigpro.2021.108341","citation_count":62,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3202332855","url":"https://openalex.org/W3202332855","query":"adversarial image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"66173981aa4b1ba5cf414e0de88f9b1cbb6f55a8","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/66173981aa4b1ba5cf414e0de88f9b1cbb6f55a8","query":"adversarial image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:11:10Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-d21c287e89b3abae","title":"Image splicing detection based on convolutional neural network with weight combination strategy","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-05-23","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5100630403","name":"Jinwei Wang","orcid":"0000-0002-9366-5671","institution_ids":["i149594827","i200845125"]},{"id":"a5088682922","name":"Qiye Ni","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i200845125"]},{"id":"a5062243742","name":"Guangjie Liu","orcid":"0000-0003-4729-7406","institution_ids":["i200845125"]},{"id":"a5102018721","name":"Xiangyang Luo","orcid":"0000-0001-6062-2950","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5044207716","name":"Sunil Kumar Jha","orcid":"0000-0002-6955-1244","institution_ids":["i200845125"]}],"institution_ids":["i149594827","i200845125"],"venue":{"id":"venue-3402a4163f184b","name":"Journal of Information Security and Applications","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.jisa.2020.102523","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3027467469","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jisa.2020.102523","citation_count":29,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3027467469","url":"https://openalex.org/W3027467469","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1016/j.jisa.2020.102523","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jisa.2020.102523","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:44Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-cafd23a5beec86ae","title":"Image splicing detection using mask-RCNN","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-01-17","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5014240079","name":"Belal Ahmed","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i212119943"]},{"id":"a5035133764","name":"T. Aaron Gulliver","orcid":"0000-0001-9919-0323","institution_ids":["i212119943"]},{"id":"a5075435260","name":"Saif alZahir","orcid":"0000-0003-1955-5834","institution_ids":["i147853995"]}],"institution_ids":["i147853995","i212119943"],"venue":{"id":"venue-9e72f28605115d","name":"Signal Image and Video Processing","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/s11760-020-01636-0","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2999170936","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11760-020-01636-0","citation_count":95,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2999170936","url":"https://openalex.org/W2999170936","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/s11760-020-01636-0","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11760-020-01636-0","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:29:48Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-a74236139480beae","title":"Leveraging Frequency Analysis for Deep Fake Image Recognition","title_zh":"","year":2020,"publication_date":"2020-03-19","abstract":"Deep neural networks can generate images that are astonishingly realistic, so much so that it is often hard for humans to distinguish them from actual photos. These achievements have been largely made possible by Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs). While deep fake images have been thoroughly investigated in the image domain--a classical approach from the area of image forensics--an analysis in the frequency domain has been missing so far. In this paper, we address this shortcoming and our results reveal that in frequency space, GAN-generated images exhibit severe artifacts that can be easily identified. We perform a comprehensive analysis, showing that these artifacts are consistent across different neural network architectures, data sets, and resolutions. In a further investigation, we demonstrate that these artifacts are caused by upsampling operations found in all current GAN architectures, indicating a structural and fundamental problem in the way images are generated via GANs. Based on this analysis, we demonstrate how the frequency representation can be used to identify deep fake images in an automated way, surpassing state-of-the-art methods.","authors":[{"id":"author-01c449c3ad1fef","name":"Joel Frank","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-197a2bc5d4cab0","name":"Thorsten Eisenhofer","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-4c97afad4f27f5","name":"Lea Schönherr","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-fa31378428e006","name":"Asja Fischer","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-57a7264ac23f88","name":"Dorothea Kolossa","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-2b93875c5192a8","name":"Thorsten Holz","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":["i4210128801","i904495901","institution:8f8dd64c6339c8ff"],"venue":{"id":"venue-icml","name":"Proceedings of the 37th International Conference on Machine Learning","short_name":"ICML","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CCF","level":"A","category":"人工智能","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"第七版（2026）","source_url":"https://www.ccf.org.cn/Academic_Evaluation/By_category/","verified_at":"2026-07-16"}]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection","synthetic_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2003.08685","arxiv_id":"2003.08685","openalex_id":"W3012033723","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2003.08685","citation_count":933,"provenance":[{"source":"authorized_seed","source_id":"curated:dcf7aae2c8590b07aff3","url":"https://openalex.org/W3012033723","query":"","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T00:00:00Z"},{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3012033723","url":"https://openalex.org/W3012033723","query":"GAN image forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3034946971","url":"https://openalex.org/W3034946971","query":"GAN image forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"322924507dfe691640d1de54f52789e296afbca3","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/322924507dfe691640d1de54f52789e296afbca3","query":"GAN image forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:10:05Z"}],"notes":""},{"id":"paper-bcd96c384dd7b5ae","title":"CNN Based Image Forgery Detection Using Pre-trained AlexNet Model","title_zh":"","year":2019,"publication_date":"2019-03-19","abstract":"Image forgery detection is an approach for detection and localization of forged component from a manipulated image. To find manipulation or tampering in the original image, an adequate number of features are required to classify the given image is either a forged or non-forged. To achieve this convolutional neural network (CNN) based pre-trained AlexNet model's deep features have been utilized which are efficient and effective, as compared to the existing state-of-the-art approaches on publicly available benchmark dataset MICC-F220. The experiment result shows that the proposed approach using a pre-trained AlexNet model based deep features with Support Vector Machine (SVM) classifier has achieved 93.94% accuracy.","authors":[{"id":"a5036570871","name":"Amit Doegar","orcid":"0000-0001-7463-432X","institution_ids":["i4210094264","i4210094717"]},{"id":"a5083745534","name":"Maitreyee Dutta","orcid":"0000-0002-2608-6821","institution_ids":["i4210094264","i4210094717"]},{"id":"a5065738622","name":"Kumar Gaurav","orcid":"0009-0008-5249-8441","institution_ids":["i4210101851"]}],"institution_ids":["i4210094264","i4210094717","i4210101851"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3128567171","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://openalex.org/W3128567171","citation_count":31,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3128567171","url":"https://openalex.org/W3128567171","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-ee9d3b0ec36656ae","title":"An Invisible Image Watermarking Based On Modified Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) Algorithm","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-eec59fde7747a3","name":"Atheer Bassel","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-79691e5880257d","name":"Md Jan Nordin","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-1f256e3846bb12","name":"Mohammed B. Abdulkareem","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-f68a7ce5e985e4","name":"International Journal of Security and Its Applications","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"1738-9976","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.14257/ijsia.2018.12.2.01","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.14257/ijsia.2018.12.2.01","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.14257/ijsia.2018.12.2.01","url":"https://doi.org/10.14257/ijsia.2018.12.2.01","query":"image watermarking @ USENIX Security","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:43:26Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-9b8b52e0523fa7ae","title":"Steganalysis Using Unsupervised End-to-End CNN Fused with Residual Image","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"","abstract":"Recently, convolutional neural networks (CNNs)has been used in the field of image steganalysis. However, there are still many deficiencies. In order to improve the detection accuracy, we propose an unsupervised end-to-end CNN to extract image features of the stego images. The end-to-end mapping can be trained to learn the most effective characteristic expression from input images to output images. By integrating hidden layers of the deep CNN, the extracted features can be considered as having characteristics of both input images and its residual images. In this way, we try to minimize the negative effect of the high-pass filtering under the condition of guaranteeing the convergence of the network. The experimental results show that the end-to-end CNN maintains good performance on BOSSBase even when the embedding rate is 0.1 bpp.","authors":[{"id":"author-d46996fb2ff348","name":"Yao Wu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-211ef14266a271","name":"Hui Li","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-0f876c46394439","name":"Junkai Yi","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"i